From e4f26718dedb7097933b789edd26e16da3969836 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Gilbert <1travisgilbert@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:40:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gpui_web): adopt a page-owned editing island as the IME
 conduit

A page may hand GPUI a visible textarea it created and placed. While the
island is live it is the window's conduit: it receives the same input,
selection, composition, paste and history listeners as the hidden
conduit, and the mirror writes the focused input handler's whole
document back to it as the smallest replacement (execCommand while
focused, so the element's own undo stack stays enabled; a plain value
write otherwise). The page owns placement and the accessible name; the
mirror never moves, restyles or renames it.

- Direction travels both ways: selectionchange imports a backward
  selection through the new set_text_selection(UTF16Selection), and the
  sync writes it back with setSelectionRange's direction.
- The mirror's own writes are recognized by state and counted as echoes,
  never imported.
- historyUndo/historyRedo from beforeinput, or from input when
  beforeinput is absent, are routed once through the keybinding path to
  the document's single history; the element's diff is never imported.
- A composition is checkpointed when it begins so its end can tell a
  commit from a cancel; the checkpoint never restores text.
- EditingIsland (adopt, set_live, counts, composing; Drop releases) is
  the public surface, and EditingIslandCounts reports what it did.
- gpui: InputHandler and EntityInputHandler gain set_text_selection,
  defaulting to set_selected_text_range.
